   "MatterHistoryActionName": "elected",
   "MatterHistoryActionText": "The Rules, Confirmations, and Public Elections Committee recommended the nominees. The President called for an election to fill a vacancy on the Property Standards and Appeals Board. Nominations previously made were: Grafton Brittle and Roger Farmer. The following vote was taken on the nominated candidates: Roger Farmer (21): Suara, Porterfield, Kimbrough, Toombs, Parker, Capp, Benedict, Webb, Eslick, Evans, Bradford, Huffman, Gregg, Welsch, Vo, Gadd, Preptit, Nash, Ellis, Styles, and Ewing; Grafton Brittle (13): Allen, Hill, Gamble, Cortese, Harrell, Cash, Kupin, Horton, Benton, Sepulveda, Rutherford, Lee, and Spain; Abstain (0). The President declared that Roger Farmer was elected to the Board.",
